WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.880
Settle in a safe resting position.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.995
Adjust pillows, blankets, and posture before beginning.

3
00:00:09.695 --> 00:00:20.485
This practice is about letting the bed carry more weight, not forcing the body to become relaxed or still.

4
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:29.227
Feel the place where the head meets support.

5
00:00:30.927 --> 00:00:35.417
Notice the size and shape of that contact.

6
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:41.447
Let the surface receive what it already receives.

7
00:00:52.276 --> 00:00:54.156
Bring attention to the shoulders.

8
00:00:55.856 --> 00:00:59.566
One may rest more fully than the other.

9
00:01:01.266 --> 00:01:06.446
Allow the difference without trying to make both sides match.

10
00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:22.516
Feel the upper back spreading across the bed.

11
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:32.081
On an exhale, notice whether even a small amount of weight is handed over.

12
00:01:33.781 --> 00:01:37.766
If not, stay with the simple contact.

13
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.840
Move to the arms.

14
00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:59.035
Sense upper arms, elbows, forearms, and hands.

15
00:02:00.735 --> 00:02:05.425
Let each region have its own weight and temperature.

16
00:02:18.059 --> 00:02:26.199
Notice the chest moving with breath and the back remaining supported beneath that movement.

17
00:02:27.899 --> 00:02:32.224
The body can move and be held at the same time.

18
00:02:44.858 --> 00:02:47.258
Feel the belly and lower ribs.

19
00:02:48.958 --> 00:02:50.438
Do not push them down.

20
00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:57.918
Let the bed receive the back of the body while the front remains free to breathe.

21
00:03:10.553 --> 00:03:15.373
Bring awareness to the lower back and pelvis.

22
00:03:17.073 --> 00:03:23.358
This may be one of the heaviest regions.

23
00:03:25.058 --> 00:03:31.163
Notice where pressure is broad, concentrated, comfortable, or unclear.

24
00:03:45.602 --> 00:03:50.402
If the position asks for a small adjustment, make it.

25
00:03:52.102 --> 00:03:57.922
Then feel the new pattern of contact rather than judging whether it is better.

26
00:04:08.751 --> 00:04:10.551
Move into the thighs.

27
00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:16.956
Let the large muscles stop performing for a few moments.

28
00:04:18.656 --> 00:04:24.356
They do not need to feel soft; they only need permission not to act.

29
00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.590
Feel the knees and lower legs.

30
00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:49.470
Notice fabric, air, warmth, coolness, and the places where the bed rises to meet them.

31
00:05:02.105 --> 00:05:06.265
Bring attention to heels and feet.

32
00:05:07.965 --> 00:05:10.605
Let their weight travel down into support.

33
00:05:12.305 --> 00:05:17.055
Toes can curl, spread, or remain as they are.

34
00:05:29.689 --> 00:05:34.729
Now sense the whole line of the body from head to feet.

35
00:05:36.429 --> 00:05:37.949
Imagine no sinking.

36
00:05:39.649 --> 00:05:44.544
Feel only the actual distribution of weight already present.

37
00:06:00.788 --> 00:06:06.448
Notice one region that still seems to hold itself away from the bed.

38
00:06:08.148 --> 00:06:15.128
Offer it the possibility of being supported, without demanding a response.

39
00:06:27.762 --> 00:06:30.442
Let three ordinary exhales pass.

40
00:06:32.142 --> 00:06:41.342
With each one, recognize a different contact area: head, torso, then legs.

41
00:06:57.587 --> 00:06:59.147
Release the scan.

42
00:07:00.847 --> 00:07:03.527
Let attention become broad and less precise.

43
00:07:05.227 --> 00:07:10.347
The bed does not need your supervision to keep carrying the body.

44
00:07:26.591 --> 00:07:30.661
If sleepiness comes, you can stop listening.

45
00:07:32.361 --> 00:07:39.051
If wakefulness remains, continue resting with the simple fact of support.

46
00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.160
Nothing had to melt or disappear.

47
00:07:53.860 --> 00:08:00.000
You practiced allowing one region at a time to be met by the bed.
